WEBVTT

00:00:00.095 --> 00:00:01.851
Here are some jobs that
are on your ballot.

00:00:02.631 --> 00:00:04.671
County assessor. Water district board.

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:06.631
Community college trustee.

00:00:07.331 --> 00:00:10.338
Superior court judge.
School board, seat four.

00:00:10.973 --> 00:00:12.265
Most people can name the president,

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.425
probably the governor, maybe one senator,

00:00:14.785 --> 00:00:17.745
and then it stops. That is not ignorance.

00:00:18.345 --> 00:00:19.785
Nobody ever handed you the list.

00:00:20.477 --> 00:00:23.627
The information exists. It is
just kept in a dozen places.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:25.847
The city clerk has the council.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:27.887
The county has the assessor.

00:00:28.287 --> 00:00:29.667
The state has the legislature.

00:00:30.227 --> 00:00:32.047
The federal election
commission has the money.

00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:34.147
None of them talk to each other.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.260
So to answer one plain
question — who represents me —

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.960
you would have to visit all
of them, and already know

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:42.844
what you were looking for.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.507
This is Empowered Essentials.

00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:50.783
Essentials starts from one piece
of information. Where you live.

00:00:51.415 --> 00:00:54.143
Your address sits inside
a stack of boundaries.

00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:56.023
A city. A school district.

00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:59.323
A county. A state house district,
a state senate district,

00:00:59.763 --> 00:01:01.843
a congressional district. They overlap,

00:01:02.123 --> 00:01:04.383
they are different
shapes, and almost none of

00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:05.723
them line up with each other.

00:01:06.361 --> 00:01:10.049
We take the address, work out
every boundary that contains it,

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.069
and hand back every
office that comes with it.

00:01:13.509 --> 00:01:17.169
Grouped by level. Local at the
top, federal at the bottom.

00:01:17.719 --> 00:01:21.004
And when there is an election running,
the people asking for those seats

00:01:21.004 --> 00:01:23.414
appear next to the people
already holding them.

00:01:24.098 --> 00:01:27.847
That list on its own is more than most
voters have ever had in one place.

00:01:28.307 --> 00:01:30.927
But a name is only the
start of a question.

00:01:31.704 --> 00:01:34.044
Open anybody on the list
and you get their profile.

00:01:34.624 --> 00:01:38.244
Who they are, which seat they
hold, and when that term runs out.

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:41.354
If the seat is on the next
ballot, the page says so,

00:01:41.654 --> 00:01:44.394
and it tells you whether the person
holding it is running again or

00:01:44.394 --> 00:01:45.654
whether it is an open seat.

00:01:46.328 --> 00:01:47.855
Under that, where they stand.

00:01:48.695 --> 00:01:51.035
These are the same issues,
on the same ladders,

00:01:51.035 --> 00:01:52.695
that the Empowered Compass uses.

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:56.555
So a stance here and a stance
there mean exactly the same thing.

00:01:57.115 --> 00:01:58.499
If you have calibrated your own compass,

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:01.959
theirs is drawn over
yours right there on their

00:02:01.959 --> 00:02:04.759
page. Same spokes, same scale.

00:02:05.546 --> 00:02:09.966
Every stance carries the reasoning
behind it and the sources under that.

00:02:09.966 --> 00:02:12.986
Nothing on a profile is
our opinion of a person.

00:02:13.526 --> 00:02:16.266
It is a position we can show our work for.

00:02:16.818 --> 00:02:19.583
And where we do not have the
evidence, we leave it empty.

00:02:20.013 --> 00:02:23.903
A blank is an honest
answer. A guess is not.

00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:27.608
Then there is the part people
most want and least often get.

00:02:28.408 --> 00:02:29.848
Who paid for the campaign.

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:33.191
Every dollar raised is
sorted into four groups.

00:02:33.991 --> 00:02:35.431
Small grassroots donations.

00:02:36.251 --> 00:02:39.471
Large individual donors.
Political action committees.

00:02:40.191 --> 00:02:43.271
And money the candidate loaned
or gave to their own campaign.

00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:46.762
Those proportions tell you
something a total never will.

00:02:47.702 --> 00:02:51.442
Two campaigns can raise the same
amount of money and be funded by

00:02:51.442 --> 00:02:52.802
entirely different people.

00:02:53.412 --> 00:02:56.510
You can open the committees one by
one and see what each of them gave.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.024
You can search the donors by name.

00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:02.396
And kept separate from all
of it, outside spending.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:07.356
Money spent for or against that candidate
by groups the candidate does not

00:03:07.356 --> 00:03:11.376
control, which is a different
thing and is worth not mixing in.

00:03:12.011 --> 00:03:13.961
All of it comes out of the public filings.

00:03:14.681 --> 00:03:16.761
Federal candidates from the
Federal Election Commission,

00:03:17.301 --> 00:03:19.421
state and local from their
own disclosure systems.

00:03:19.941 --> 00:03:21.521
We are not revealing anything.

00:03:21.521 --> 00:03:24.363
We are putting it where a
person can actually read it.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.499
For the officials who vote
on things, we show the votes.

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:31.199
The bill, what it did,
and which way they went.

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:35.390
What somebody says they believe and
what they voted for are two different

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:39.590
records. Essentials puts
both on one page and lets you

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.146
notice the distance yourself.

00:03:41.658 --> 00:03:45.018
Now the honest part.
Essentials is in alpha.

00:03:45.842 --> 00:03:48.831
Type any address in the United States
and you will get your members of

00:03:48.831 --> 00:03:51.011
Congress, and the people
running for the House.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.891
That part works everywhere.

00:03:53.675 --> 00:03:56.923
The full picture — every office
from the city council up —

00:03:56.923 --> 00:03:58.283
lives in our alpha communities.

00:03:58.913 --> 00:04:01.323
Those are the places we have taken in,

00:04:01.603 --> 00:04:03.323
curated, and checked by hand.

00:04:03.895 --> 00:04:07.510
And a smaller set of those again have
stances on their local officials,

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.550
because reading a council member's
record takes longer than listing one.

00:04:12.182 --> 00:04:16.370
Both lists grow every week, and
they grow slowly on purpose.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:20.570
Each one is a real roster,
read out of a real clerk's

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.550
office. Not a scrape and a hope.

00:04:23.143 --> 00:04:25.863
If your area is not covered
yet, the site says so.

00:04:26.283 --> 00:04:30.103
We would rather tell you what is
missing than show you a thin answer and

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.383
let you think it was the whole one.

00:04:31.921 --> 00:04:34.921
It is worth saying why the bottom
of the ballot gets this much work.

00:04:35.412 --> 00:04:38.832
Those offices decide most
of what you actually touch.

00:04:39.672 --> 00:04:41.392
Your zoning. Your school day.

00:04:41.692 --> 00:04:46.572
Your water bill. What your house is
assessed at. Who hears your case.

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.118
And they are won with the fewest votes.

00:04:49.118 --> 00:04:52.518
A council seat can turn on
a couple of hundred people.

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:56.258
Which means the bottom of the
ballot is exactly where one informed

00:04:56.258 --> 00:04:57.998
voter counts for the most.

00:04:58.651 --> 00:05:02.431
The reason people vote the top of
the ballot and guess the rest is not

00:05:02.431 --> 00:05:05.831
apathy. It is that the rest
was never made readable.

00:05:06.838 --> 00:05:10.603
This one is live today, at
essentials dot empowered dot vote.

00:05:11.219 --> 00:05:14.704
Put in your address once. Meet
everybody who represents you.

00:05:15.144 --> 00:05:17.564
Then look at where they
stand, and who funds them,

00:05:17.564 --> 00:05:19.304
and decide what you think.

00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:21.532
That is Empowered Essentials.

00:05:22.592 --> 00:05:24.112
Go find out who is on your ballot.
